      "text": "Hey there, how are you?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 8.251,
      "end": 12.511,
      "text": "Chemical drain cleaners often don't reach the real clog. Have you tried a plunger?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 16.716,
      "end": 22.766,
      "text": "A small cup plunger works on sinks too. Fill the sink a little so it seals, and give it some firm pumps."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 26.13,
      "end": 31.43,
      "text": "Then check the U shaped pipe under the sink. Put a bucket underneath, unscrew it, and clean out the gunk."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 34.453,
      "end": 39.183,
      "text": "It is, honestly. Wear gloves. But it's the most common spot for grease and food to build up."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 45.026,
      "end": 49.266,
      "text": "You'll be fine. It's one of those jobs that looks scary and takes ten minutes."
    }
